    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Fixes MiniMax-M3 tool calls losing all parameters when the model elides an opening parameter tag\n- `_parse_invoke_params` previously stopped at the first non-element text and returned no parameters; now `_recover_untagged_param` extracts the parameter name from the bare closing tag and treats preceding text as the value\n- This allows later well-formed parameter elements to be parsed normally\n\n## Context\n\nAfter #59743/#59744 removed the Rust parser bridge, the remaining issue is that `_parse_invoke_params` in `vllm/parser/minimax_m3.py` stops at the first malformed element. When the model emits `value]<]minimax[>[</name>` instead of `]<]minimax[>[<name>value]<]minimax[>[</name>`, the parser returns `{}` for arguments, dropping all parameters — including subsequent well-formed ones.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Verify with MiniMax-M3 model, streaming + tools — tool calls should no longer be lost when the model skips an opening parameter tag\n- [ ] Verify well-formed tool call output is unchanged\n- [ ] Verify non-streaming path is also fixed (same parser)\n\n## Notes\n\n- No duplicate PR exists for this issue\n- AI assistance was used in developing this fix\n- This is a model-specific fix in `vllm/parser/minimax_m3.py`, per the AGENTS.md guideline\n\nFixes https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/52613\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
